The problem requires determining the minimum number of subarrays needed to partition an array such that each subarray is sorted in non-decreasing order. The solution involves counting the number of times a new subarray must start as we traverse the array, which can be efficiently done by tracking the maximum value encountered so far. Each time a number is less than this maximum, a new subarray begins, incrementing the partition count.

```json
